# bat configuration
# Note: `alias cat='bat --paging=never'` in .zshrc still works; --paging here
# makes plain `bat` behave the same way.
--paging=never
--style=numbers,changes,header

# NB: pinned, NOT `--theme=auto`. Two reasons, both found by testing rather than
# assuming:
#
#   1. `auto` asks the terminal for its background over OSC 11. When that query
#      cannot be answered - a pipe, a non-TTY, a terminal that does not reply -
#      bat silently falls back to its BUILT-IN default (Monokai Extended) and
#      ignores --theme-light/--theme-dark entirely. Verified: with
#      --theme=auto set, output was byte-identical to Monokai Extended, not to
#      either configured theme. A theme setting that quietly does nothing is
#      exactly the failure mode this repo keeps running into.
#   2. There is nothing to switch between any more. ghostty is pinned to
#      `theme = catppuccin-latte`, so the terminal background is a known, fixed,
#      light colour. `auto` was solving a problem that no longer exists.
#
# Also: this was the last item of "deferred theming work" and it needed no work
# at all - bat has bundled Catppuccin since 0.24, so there is no .tmTheme to
# vendor and no `bat cache --build` hook to add. Check `bat --list-themes`
# before assuming a theme needs shipping.
--theme="Catppuccin Latte"
